From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:55:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 164/164] PC5: Wine's XACT sound engine no longer divides by
 zero for a cue whose sound hasn't started (Wine patch 1036)

FACTCue_GetProperties divided each track's length by its wave's sample rate, and a track whose wave hadn't started yet has no wave, so the rate was 0. Saints Row 2 asks for its cutscene cues' properties as they start: xactengine3_2.dll stopped with an integer division by zero on the sound thread while it held the engine's lock, and the game froze after character creation or a skipped cutscene. Such a track's properties now stay 0.
---
 ...ave-hasn-t-started-has-no-properties.patch | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1036-faudio-a-cue-s-track-whose-wave-hasn-t-started-has-no-properties.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1036-faudio-a-cue-s-track-whose-wave-hasn-t-started-has-no-properties.patch b/wine/patches/1036-faudio-a-cue-s-track-whose-wave-hasn-t-started-has-no-properties.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..338ca9c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1036-faudio-a-cue-s-track-whose-wave-hasn-t-started-has-no-properties.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] faudio: A cue's track whose wave hasn't started has no
+ properties.
+
+FACTCue_GetProperties describes each track's wave, and a track whose
+play event is still waiting has none yet. FACTWave_GetProperties then
+left the properties empty (it returns 1 for no wave, which nothing
+checked; the assert is compiled out), and the track's duration was
+divided by a sample rate of 0. Saints Row 2 asks for its cutscene cues'
+properties as they start: xactengine3_2.dll stopped with an integer
+division by zero (+0x4e9e) on the sound thread, which was holding the
+engine's lock, so the game froze after character creation or when a
+cutscene was skipped, with the cutscene's voices missing.
+
+Such a track's properties now stay 0, as they were allocated; a track
+with a wave is described as before.
+---
+ libs/faudio/src/FACT.c | 11 +++++++++--
+ 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/libs/faudio/src/FACT.c b/libs/faudio/src/FACT.c
+index ae299fb..04fb725 100644
+--- a/libs/faudio/src/FACT.c
++++ b/libs/faudio/src/FACT.c
+@@ -2756,8 +2756,15 @@ uint32_t FACTCue_GetProperties(
+ 			FACTTrackProperties *track_props = &sndProps->arrTrackProperties[i];
+ 			FACTTrackInstance *track = &pCue->playingSound->tracks[i];
+ 
+-			FAudio_assert(track->activeWave.wave);
+-			FACTWave_GetProperties(track->activeWave.wave, &waveProps);
++			/* A track whose wave hasn't started yet (its play event is
++			 * still waiting) has no wave to describe: its properties stay
++			 * 0, instead of a division by a sample rate of 0.
++			 */
++			if (	FACTWave_GetProperties(track->activeWave.wave, &waveProps) != FAUDIO_OK ||
++				waveProps.properties.format.nSamplesPerSec == 0	)
++			{
++				continue;
++			}
+ 
+ 			track_props->duration = (waveProps.properties.durationInSamples * 1000)
+ 				/ waveProps.properties.format.nSamplesPerSec;
